{
  "about": "US library pages (owner decisions, 23 November 2026), built by tools/seo/build-pages.mjs with tools/seo/check-pages.mjs. Every US BiblioCommons library offered when finding a library (server/data/us-catalogs-listed.json lists it and its removed list does not) has a page at /libraries/<slug>, except the entries in leftOut, with the directory's facts (the city from shared/seo-us-cities.json where the IMLS survey gives the system's own city) and the first ten books of shared/us-book-pool.json to check live, on a reader's tap. Nothing is checked in advance: BiblioCommons' terms forbid automated collection, and its availability is never stored (server/data/catalog-policies.json). libraries is generated, never typed: run node tools/seo/us-pages.mjs after the listed file or leftOut changes (a test fails until it is current). A slug, once given, is kept: it is the library's /select/ link name when the page is added (the four California guides keep their guide slug; a hash suffix is dropped). state is the directory's state; on is the date the page was added or its state changed. leftOut is kept by hand: an entry that is not one public library system (a school, a college, a kids' catalog, a consortium's shared catalog whose member libraries have their own pages; sameCatalogAs names a page with the same location list) or a catalog the app can no longer read, with the reason and date. firstStates: the states /libraries shows first; the others follow alphabetically.",
